# Performance Rules

- Prefer Next.js Server Components by default.
- Use Client Components only where browser interactivity/state requires them.
- Avoid fetching entire catalogs to the browser.
- Use pagination for large datasets.
- Keep filters/sorting URL-driven and server-efficient.
- Avoid N+1 database queries.
- Optimize images and avoid unnecessary client-side JavaScript.
- Avoid large global state stores unless justified.
- Use caching/revalidation deliberately.
- Do not add animation or effects that materially hurt performance.
- Measure before introducing complex optimization.
- PC Builder must fetch only relevant component candidates.
